         The Town Clerk is: Chief Election Official: Oversees all elections, voter registration sessions, certifies nomination papers, initiative petitions and conducts annual town census Recording Officer: Records, certifies and maintains all official actions of the town Registry of Vital Statistics: Registers all birth, marriage, and death records occurring with the community Public Records Officer: Administers the oath of office to all elected and appointed members. Posts all meetings of government bodies. Provides certified copies of vital records. Maintains records of all local bylaws. Licensing Officer: Issues licenses: marriage, dog and permits for raffles and bazaars. The Town Clerk is elected every three years. ALL ELECTIONS ARE HELD AT 48 HIGH ST., SHEPARD BLDG. GYM Annual Town Election:  Held the first Tuesday of May Annual Town Meeting:  Held the second Thursday of June 
     

 
